title: 'cumulus: hold slot-based block building on an unincluded runtime upgrade'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    The slot-based collator no longer builds on a block that applies a runtime upgrade until that
    block is included. It stops iterating cores after building such a block. While one is
    unincluded, it reruns the parent search under the scheduling rules of the upgrade's parent:
    it waits while the upgrade can still be backed, and builds below it once it expires. This
    avoids candidates that the new or old validation code rejects when the upgrade changes the
    scheduling format, such as a switch from V2 to V3.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
